WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.140
This is every country in the world… by Wendover
Productions.

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:08.029
We’ll start with
Afghanistan, the first country alphabetically.

00:00:08.029 --> 00:00:11.870
Afghanistan is one of the few countries worldwide
to be offset from Greenwich Mean Time by a

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:15.750
30 minute interval, its at GMT +4:30, while
China

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.920
is one of the many countries to only have
one timezone… except its ginormous.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:21.680
It aligns to GMT
+ 8 so that means that stepping over the 47

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.870
mile long Afghanistan-China border jumps you
forward by 3.5 hours.

00:00:25.870 --> 00:00:28.910
That’s the largest single time zone jump
on earth.

00:00:28.910 --> 00:00:31.960
China in all its craziness
has rather ambitious plans to build a high-speed

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:36.230
railroad from Beijing, up across the Bering
Strait, and down into the United States, which

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:40.149
happens to be the home of 41% of Wendover
Productions viewers.

00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:44.030
Up in the north-west of the US, Point Roberts,
a part of the mainland US, is

00:00:44.030 --> 00:00:47.701
cut off from the US by Canada and since it
doesn’t have a high-school, students have

00:00:47.701 --> 00:00:50.620
to cross
into Canada then back into the US each day

00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.170
on their way to school.

00:00:52.170 --> 00:00:54.860
Canada happens to be the
second largest country on earth and has more

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:57.040
lakes than the rest of the world combined.

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:59.420
Its so
huge, in fact, that its easternmost point

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:02.420
is closer to Croatia than it is to Vancouver.

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:04.960
One of
Croatia’s thousands of islands is Rab, the

00:01:04.960 --> 00:01:07.210
birthplace of the sculptor Marinas who went
on and

00:01:07.210 --> 00:01:11.970
founded San Marino, the fifth smallest country
in the world and one of three to be completely

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.439
surrounded by another country.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:16.090
One of the others is the Vatican—the smallest
sovereign state in

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:20.759
the world—and there’s also Lesotho, which
is home to one of Africa’s seven ski resorts.

00:01:20.759 --> 00:01:23.240
Lesotho
is of course surrounded by South Africa which

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.840
is the only country in the world to have three
capitals—Cape Town is the seat of the Parliament,

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:32.249
Pretoria is the home of the president, and
Bloemfontein is the judicial capital.

00:01:32.249 --> 00:01:34.899
South Africa also almost completely surrounds
another

00:01:34.899 --> 00:01:39.509
country—Swaziland, where roads are so bad
that two of the last four transport ministers

00:01:39.509 --> 00:01:40.860
died in
car accidents.

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:44.490
While mostly surrounded by South Africa, Swaziland’s
eastern border is with

00:01:44.490 --> 00:01:49.279
Mozambique, whose name scores higher in scrabble
than any other one-word country, but in

00:01:49.279 --> 00:01:53.840
second place for scrabble is Kyrgyzstan which
is home to six enclaves, the smallest of which

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:56.979
is
part of Uzbekistan and is only 2 miles wide.

00:01:56.979 --> 00:01:59.940
In Uzbekistan, no river leads to the Ocean—they
all

00:01:59.940 --> 00:02:03.869
drain into endorheic basins where all the
water evaporates out.

00:02:03.869 --> 00:02:07.630
Uzbekistan is one of only two
countries worldwide to be double-landlocked—as

00:02:07.630 --> 00:02:10.690
in, landlocked by landlocked countries.

00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:13.420
In this
case, every surrounding country of Uzbekistan

00:02:13.420 --> 00:02:19.100
also ends in -stan—Kazakhstan, Tajikistan,
Kyrgyzstan, Afghanistan,and Turkmenistan.

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:23.320
The other double-landlocked country is
Liechtenstein—a tiny and historically neutral

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:24.320
nation.

00:02:24.320 --> 00:02:28.700
In their last military engagement in 1886,
none of the 80 soldiers were injured or killed,

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:31.500
and they actually returned with 81 people
since

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:34.190
they made a “new italian friend.”

00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:37.080
Italy is home to the Breuil Cervinia ski resort
where you can

00:02:37.080 --> 00:02:39.580
ski across the border into Switzerland.

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:42.720
Switzerland is rather paranoid about war to
the extent that

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:47.980
3,000 points of entry into the country are
rigged to blow at an instant in case of invasion.

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:52.150
Switzerland is also home to one end of the
shortest regularly-scheduled commercial international

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:57.000
flight in the world—a six minute, 10 mile
jaunt over to Germany where its not actually

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.680
illegal to
escape prison.

00:02:58.680 --> 00:03:01.080
Seriously—they say its only human nature.

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.170
Germany is home to half of one of the
world’s few internationally divided islands,

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:07.620
and the Polish side of this island, despite
being only

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:12.950
200 feet from mainland Poland, is not connected
by any bridges to Poland, so just like point

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:17.280
Roberts, residents have to cross international
borders to get to their own country.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:19.520
Poland also
happens to have been a part of Sweden’s

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:22.760
monarchy for a brief eight years in the 16th
century.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:28.020
Sweden has an internationally divided island
too, and this one is a mere 7 acres large.

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:30.510
The border
looks like this because Finland accidentally

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:33.180
built a lighthouse in Swedish territory and
so they

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.980
just readjusted the border to make everyone
happy.

00:03:35.980 --> 00:03:43.350
Finland has exactly 187,888 lakes, and its
northernmost point is actually closer to Greenland

00:03:43.350 --> 00:03:45.990
than Poland due to the curvature of the earth.

00:03:45.990 --> 00:03:49.830
Greenland isn’t actually a country so I’m
not allowed to talk about it—its a dependency

00:03:49.830 --> 00:03:52.180
of
Denmark, where its impossible to be more than

00:03:52.180 --> 00:03:53.570
30 miles from the ocean.

00:03:53.570 --> 00:03:57.860
The wife of Denmark’s Crown Prince, Crown
Princess Mary, was born in Australia which

00:03:57.860 --> 00:04:02.310
is the 6th largest country on earth and is
home to the longest fence in the world—a

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:07.090
3,500 mile structure to keep wild dogs out
of the the fertile south-east region.

00:04:07.090 --> 00:04:13.111
The middle of Australia also has practically
nobody and nothing in it except a 297 mile

00:04:13.111 --> 00:04:16.160
long precisely straight section of railroad
track.

00:04:16.160 --> 00:04:20.469
Australia freed the country of Brunei from
occupation back in WWII which is one of the

00:04:20.469 --> 00:04:24.629
few countries worldwide to be comprised of
two comparably sized sections.

00:04:24.629 --> 00:04:28.110
St Kitts and Nevis is
also split into two but that’s because its

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:30.900
a two island nation and also the smallest
country in the

00:04:30.900 --> 00:04:32.110
Americas.

00:04:32.110 --> 00:04:36.999
In Saint Kitts and Nevis you can gain citizenship
by making a $400 thousand real estate investment

00:04:36.999 --> 00:04:40.789
much like Bulgaria, where people nod up and
down to signify no and shake left

00:04:40.789 --> 00:04:42.139
and right to mean yes.

00:04:42.139 --> 00:04:45.050
Bulgaria is one of the few countries to have
an embassy in North Korea

00:04:45.050 --> 00:04:49.699
which created its own time zone in 2015 for
no real reason than to be different.

00:04:49.699 --> 00:04:52.680
North Korea is
only separated by one country from Norway,

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:54.440
where more than half the population lives
below

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:55.590
this line.

00:04:55.590 --> 00:04:58.410
Between Norway and North Korea is of course
Russia—the largest country in the

00:04:58.410 --> 00:04:59.410
world.

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:02.490
Its easternmost point is, in fact, closer
to Mexico than Moscow.

00:05:02.490 --> 00:05:05.280
Mexico once had three
different presidents in one hour during a

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:07.879
military coup, but also accustomed to short
regimes is

00:05:07.879 --> 00:05:12.749
Alsace-Lorraine in France which was an fully-recognized
independent country for 12 short days

00:05:12.749 --> 00:05:15.960
between being part of Germany and France at
the end of World War One.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:19.560
France, of course, had
an enormous empire including Algeria which

00:05:19.560 --> 00:05:22.080
is the largest country in Africa and unlike
some of

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:24.759
its neighboring countries, is quite nice to
women.

00:05:24.759 --> 00:05:27.570
70% of the countries lawyers are female.

00:05:27.570 --> 00:05:29.710
Right
next door to Algeria is Morocco which has

00:05:29.710 --> 00:05:32.759
de facto control of some of Western Sahara,
a place

00:05:32.759 --> 00:05:34.229
thats not really part of any country.

00:05:34.229 --> 00:05:36.529
That’s why its always blank on data maps.

00:05:36.529 --> 00:05:39.919
Morocco
surrounds two Spanish exclaves, Ceuta and

00:05:39.919 --> 00:05:42.370
Melilla, which are politically part of mainland
Spain,

00:05:42.370 --> 00:05:46.219
rather than overseas territories, despite
being in Northern Africa.

00:05:46.219 --> 00:05:49.909
Spain once had an enormous
empire, part of which was Micronesia which

00:05:49.909 --> 00:05:52.779
is now a US associated state, meaning they’re
an

00:05:52.779 --> 00:05:56.319
independent nation but the US covers defense
and funding.

00:05:56.319 --> 00:06:00.789
Micronesian citizens can join the US
military without becoming a US resident—a

00:06:00.789 --> 00:06:03.470
right only given to citizens of freely associated
states.

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:05.909
Their currency is also the US dollar.

00:06:05.909 --> 00:06:08.659
Palau is also a nearby US associated state
which is

00:06:08.659 --> 00:06:13.360
often compared to Fiji since they’re both
idillic pacific island destinations even though

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:15.770
they're
over 3,500 miles apart.

00:06:15.770 --> 00:06:19.669
Fiji was a British colony up until 1970 and
you have no idea how hard it

00:06:19.669 --> 00:06:21.900
was to avoid using this transition up until
now.

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:24.559
I could’ve used it with Nauru, St Kitts
and Nevis,

00:06:24.559 --> 00:06:28.349
Brunei, Australia, South Africa, Canada, the
United States, and Afghanistan but I kept

00:06:28.349 --> 00:06:29.349
it for now.

00:06:29.349 --> 00:06:33.349
The UK is home to the shortest regularly scheduled
commercial flight in the world between

00:06:33.349 --> 00:06:36.220
Westray and Papa Westray in the Scottish isles.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:41.460
It costs 17 pounds, takes 53 seconds, and
traverses only 1.7 miles.

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:45.529
The UK has two exclaves—both of which are
overseas territories.

00:06:45.529 --> 00:06:46.833
One
is Gibraltar, right across from Ceuta, and

00:06:46.833 --> 00:06:50.749
the the other is Akrotiri and Dhekelia on
the island of

00:06:50.749 --> 00:06:51.749
Cyprus.

00:06:51.749 --> 00:06:56.199
There are border control agents from three
countries on Cyprus, the UK, Cyprus, and

00:06:56.199 --> 00:06:57.389
Turkey.

00:06:57.389 --> 00:07:01.229
Northern Cyprus is a self-declared state only
recognized by Turkey who helps them keep

00:07:01.229 --> 00:07:05.330
control of the territory with a heavy military
presence and border control agents.

00:07:05.330 --> 00:07:07.949
Istanbul,
Turkey, is the only city on the planet to

00:07:07.949 --> 00:07:10.270
span two continents—Europe and Asia—although
there

00:07:10.270 --> 00:07:12.680
are plenty of countries on two continents.

00:07:12.680 --> 00:07:15.559
In Egypt, the Sinai peninsula sits in Asia
while the rest

00:07:15.559 --> 00:07:16.889
is in Africa.

00:07:16.889 --> 00:07:20.800
Just past the southern border of Egypt is
Bir Tawil, a piece of land claimed by no

00:07:20.800 --> 00:07:24.499
country since Egypt and Sudan disagree on
where their borders are.

00:07:24.499 --> 00:07:28.369
Sudan recently split into two
and created South Sudan—the world’s youngest

00:07:28.369 --> 00:07:29.749
UN recognized country.

00:07:29.749 --> 00:07:33.860
The second youngest
country is Serbia which, up until 2006, was

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:36.870
called Serbia and Montenegro but split after
a

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:37.870
referendum.

00:07:37.870 --> 00:07:41.830
Montenegro also happens to be a town in Costa
Rica where about 100 people live.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:46.900
The capital of Costa Rica, San Jose, only
allows car owners to drive 6 days a week to

00:07:46.900 --> 00:07:49.300
fight
pollution and congestion, so the last digit

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:52.099
of license plates correspond to their banned
day.

00:07:52.099 --> 00:07:54.339
Costa
Rica’s southern border is with Panama, home

00:07:54.339 --> 00:07:57.020
to the Panama Canal which, counterintuitively,
has

00:07:57.020 --> 00:08:01.449
its Atlantic end, the ocean to the east, to
the west, and its Pacific end, the ocean to

00:08:01.449 --> 00:08:03.220
the west, to the
east.

00:08:03.220 --> 00:08:07.220
Panama’s southern border is with Colombia
but there's not one road crossing this 50

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:09.490
mile
jungle which means its impossible to drive

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:11.629
between North and South America.

00:08:11.629 --> 00:08:14.339
You probably
know that Colombia was once part of Spain

00:08:14.339 --> 00:08:15.339
but so was the Netherlands.

00:08:15.339 --> 00:08:17.340
It was called the Spanish
Netherlands.

00:08:17.340 --> 00:08:20.999
The Netherlands is also home to Baarle-Nassau,
one of the most messed up borders

00:08:20.999 --> 00:08:21.999
in the world.

00:08:21.999 --> 00:08:26.000
Belgium is well known for having a UN headquarters,
and so does Nairobi, Kenya

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:28.749
—the suspected birthplace of the human race.

00:08:28.749 --> 00:08:34.500
Kenya’s northern neighbor is Somalia, which
received its first ATM machine in 2014.

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:37.380
Somalia has had three separate wars with Ethiopia
in the

00:08:37.380 --> 00:08:41.789
last century, and Ethiopia national airline
was the second in the world to receive the

00:08:41.789 --> 00:08:45.170
787
Dreamliner despite being the 13th poorest

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:46.170
country.

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:50.471
Ethiopia also has another one of those
internationally divided islands, this one

00:08:50.471 --> 00:08:52.910
with Djibouti, which is home to the lowest
point in

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:57.010
Africa, Lake Assal, at 509 feet below sea
level.

00:08:57.010 --> 00:08:59.630
Djibouti also hosts the only US military base
in

00:08:59.630 --> 00:09:04.120
Africa, and Israel hosts one of the smallest
ones, Dimona Radar Base.

00:09:04.120 --> 00:09:08.480
Despite being a middle eastern country, Israel
competes in Eurovision and many European sports

00:09:08.480 --> 00:09:11.490
leagues since they’re
culturally much closer to Europe than the

00:09:11.490 --> 00:09:12.490
middle-east.

00:09:12.490 --> 00:09:16.352
Israel has one of the weirder international
borders with Palestine which is only a country

00:09:16.352 --> 00:09:17.810
depending on who you ask.

00:09:17.810 --> 00:09:20.520
The largest
Palestinian community outside the Arab world

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:22.650
is in Chile which is one of the only countries
to

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:25.420
have a government sponsored UFO research organization.

00:09:25.420 --> 00:09:28.970
Chile is the southernmost mainland
country in the world but doesn’t have the

00:09:28.970 --> 00:09:30.890
southernmost commercial airport.

00:09:30.890 --> 00:09:33.510
That title goes to
Argentina with their Ushuaia – Malvinas

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:34.670
International Airport.

00:09:34.670 --> 00:09:38.030
This (Iguazu Falls) spectacular
waterfall is the border between Argentina

00:09:38.030 --> 00:09:41.150
and Brazil which is home to the Amazon River,
which

00:09:41.150 --> 00:09:43.110
doesn’t have a single bridge over it.

00:09:43.110 --> 00:09:46.310
Not one—its just in an area where practically
nobody lives.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:51.420
Recife, Brazil is closer to Dakar, Senegal
than to Porte Alegre in South-western Brazil.

00:09:51.420 --> 00:09:54.080
Just off
the coast of Senegal is Cape Verde which is

00:09:54.080 --> 00:09:55.180
pretty much paradise.

00:09:55.180 --> 00:09:59.490
They have a high human
development index score, high GDP, high literacy

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:01.230
rate, and the lowest recorded temperature
in

00:10:01.230 --> 00:10:03.900
history there was 50 degrees fahrenheit.

00:10:03.900 --> 00:10:06.120
As a former Portuguese colony, Cape Verde
speaks

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:11.270
Portuguese which is the 6th most spoken language
in the world even though its origin country,

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:13.110
Portugal, is smaller than Kentucky.

00:10:13.110 --> 00:10:16.120
They just had an enormous empire, which for
a while

00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:20.800
included Indonesia, which has another one
of those internationally divided islands with

00:10:20.800 --> 00:10:23.440
Papau
New Guinea, similar to Hispaniola island which

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:26.260
is divided between Haiti and the Dominican
Republic.

00:10:26.260 --> 00:10:31.130
Hispaniola is the 22nd largest island in the
world but Madagascar is number four.

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:33.580
Its
also the largest single-island-country.

00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:36.920
85 million years ago Madagascar was connected
to India

00:10:36.920 --> 00:10:41.980
before the continents shifted but Sri Lanka
was connected to India as recently as 1480

00:10:41.980 --> 00:10:45.020
via a land
bridge that has since eroded.

00:10:45.020 --> 00:10:48.350
Sri Lanka is just north of the equator but
right on the equator is

00:10:48.350 --> 00:10:49.350
Ecuador.

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:53.900
Its capital, Quito, is only 20 miles from
the equator so its day length varies by only

00:10:53.900 --> 00:10:56.120
15
minutes between winter and summer.

00:10:56.120 --> 00:10:58.730
Although, since the country is split by the
equator, winter

00:10:58.730 --> 00:11:02.450
and summer happens at the same time in the
same country.

00:11:02.450 --> 00:11:06.240
Ecuador is one of 30 countries to have an
antarctic research base and right next door

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:08.600
to
Ecuador’s base is Peru’s.

00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:12.780
Copacabana, not that one, this one, in Bolivia,
can only be reached by

00:11:12.780 --> 00:11:14.610
driving through Peru.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:18.710
Bolivia, despite being a landlocked country,
maintains a 5,000 person

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:24.100
Navy, although Mongolia, also a landlocked
country, maintains a navy that has one ship—a

00:11:24.100 --> 00:11:27.040
tugboat—and seven total sailors.

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:30.010
Mongolia is also the least dense country on
the planet with only

00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:31.620
5 people per square mile.

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:34.610
While they may seem un-intimidating now, the
Mongolian empire was

00:11:34.610 --> 00:11:38.240
once, the largest contiguous land empire in
history.

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:42.950
Part of that empire was Cambodia, which has
changed its name six times in the last 65

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:43.950
years.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:47.010
95% of Cambodia’s population is Theravada
Buddhist.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:50.450
The other major branch of buddhism is Mahayana
Buddhism which is practiced in

00:11:50.450 --> 00:11:56.630
Japan where, out of its total population of
126 million, they had three gun murders in

00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:57.630
2012.

00:11:57.630 --> 00:12:01.820
Iceland, however, can top that, because they
had one murder total in 2012.

00:12:01.820 --> 00:12:04.170
Of course, Iceland
doesn’t have a huge population which makes

00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:07.220
it less impressive until you consider that
30% of

00:12:07.220 --> 00:12:09.010
Iceland’s residents own guns.

00:12:09.010 --> 00:12:12.860
60% of that population, however, lives in
this circle.

00:12:12.860 --> 00:12:15.800
Iceland was
also the first country to recognize Armenia’s

00:12:15.800 --> 00:12:20.180
independence, and Armenia separates Azerbaijan
from its Nakhchivan exclave and since the

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:23.510
Armenia-Azerbaijan border is closed, residents
of

00:12:23.510 --> 00:12:27.600
Nakhchivan have to go all the way around Armenia
to get to to their own country.

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:29.900
Azerbaijan's
national soccer team has played Andorra's

00:12:29.900 --> 00:12:32.580
five times in the past few decades and four
of those

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:35.380
games have ended in a 0-0 tie.

00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:38.130
Andorra is the largest country in the world
to not have an airport

00:12:38.130 --> 00:12:41.770
which is less impressive when you consider
that they’re the 19th smallest in the world.

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:43.370
The
smallest country in the world to have a major

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:46.270
international airport is the Maldives, the
8th

00:12:46.270 --> 00:12:47.270
smallest country.

00:12:47.270 --> 00:12:51.690
This airport has dozens of destinations and
is on a small island with no land

00:12:51.690 --> 00:12:55.840
connections to other islands which means once
you land you have to either take a boat or

00:12:55.840 --> 00:12:57.860
seaplane to your destination.

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:00.850
One of the airport’s destinations is Kuala
Lumpur in Malaysia

00:13:00.850 --> 00:13:05.980
which is home to world's largest roundabout
in Putrajaya at 2 miles in diameter.

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:09.010
Malaysia is the
only country connected by road to Singapore,

00:13:09.010 --> 00:13:11.140
the largest surviving city-state in the world.

00:13:11.140 --> 00:13:15.560
Despite having hundreds of skyscrapers, Singapore
is not the densest country in the world.

00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:17.940
That
title goes to Monaco which is less than one

00:13:17.940 --> 00:13:19.570
square mile large.

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:23.760
Monaco has no income tax, much
like the Bahamas, which is one of two countries

00:13:23.760 --> 00:13:27.710
whose official name starts with the word
“the”, the other one being the Gambia.

00:13:27.710 --> 00:13:30.280
The Gambia’s interesting shape comes from
the flow of

00:13:30.280 --> 00:13:35.030
the river Gambia whose watershed reaches all
the way to Guinea which is one of three countries

00:13:35.030 --> 00:13:36.880
to have the word Guinea in its name.

00:13:36.880 --> 00:13:39.540
The other two are Guinea-Bissau and Equatorial
Guinea.

00:13:39.540 --> 00:13:43.290
Guinea was once the word for the entire west-african
region so when these countries became

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:47.540
independent from their colonizers many chose
to include “guinea” in their names.

00:13:47.540 --> 00:13:49.790
Equatorial
Guinea’s capital actually isn’t on the

00:13:49.790 --> 00:13:52.920
mainland—its on an offshore island—and,
despite its name,

00:13:52.920 --> 00:13:57.380
the equator doesn’t intersect Equatorial
Guinea but the country is on both sides of

00:13:57.380 --> 00:14:00.080
the equator
since they have sovereignty over Annobón

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:01.660
island to the south of the equator.

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:04.860
This is similar to
Kiribati—a nation comprising of a few dozen

00:14:04.860 --> 00:14:06.200
islands in the Pacific.

00:14:06.200 --> 00:14:09.960
Kiribati is the first place on
earth to experience New Year’s since their

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:14.070
time zone is UTC +14—a time zone exclusive
to

00:14:14.070 --> 00:14:15.180
these islands.

00:14:15.180 --> 00:14:19.130
Kiribati is close friends with Cuba since
Cuba sent doctors to the islands who

00:14:19.130 --> 00:14:22.000
reduced the child mortality rate by 80%.

00:14:22.000 --> 00:14:24.740
Cuba—the only Caribbean island to have a
commercial

00:14:24.740 --> 00:14:27.990
railroad—is one of the few remaining communist
states.

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:32.230
One of the others is Laos—the only
landlocked country in south-east Asia—which

00:14:32.230 --> 00:14:36.940
borders Vietnam—also communist and the 14th
most populous country in the world despite

00:14:36.940 --> 00:14:39.310
having the size of about New Mexico.

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:41.750
Vietnam is
good political friends with Venezuela who

00:14:41.750 --> 00:14:43.980
is not great friends with bordering Guyana
since

00:14:43.980 --> 00:14:48.220
Guyana thinks the border looks like this and
Venezuela thinks the border looks like this.

00:14:48.220 --> 00:14:50.591
Guyana
—the only English-speaking country in South

00:14:50.591 --> 00:14:55.650
America—borders Suriname—the smallest
country in South America and the only country

00:14:55.650 --> 00:14:58.990
other than the Netherlands whose sole primary
language is Dutch.

00:14:58.990 --> 00:15:03.570
Suriname was our 98th country so that means
that we’re halfway through and that that’s

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:09.240
the end of part one of Every Country in the
World, however, part two will be out on Tuesday,

